{"id":"cmpl-geulpu-31","object":"text_completion","created":1791990928,"model":"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B-Q8_0","choices":[{"index":0,"text":"\nOkay, so I need to figure out how much change Alice gets after buying pens and notebooks. Let me see. The problem says that pens cost $5 each and notebooks cost $21 each. Alice buys 12 pens and 5 notebooks and pays with a $500 bill. I need to find out how much change she receives.\n\nFirst, I should calculate the total cost of the pens. Since each pen is $5 and she buys 12 of them, I can multiply 12 by 5. Let me write that down: 12 * 5. Hmm, 12 times 5 is 60. So, the pens cost her $60 in total.\n\nNext, I need to calculate the total cost of the notebooks. Each notebook is $21, and she buys 5 of them. So, I should multiply 5 by 21. Let me do that: 5 * 21. Hmm, 5 times 20 is 100, and 5 times 1 is 5, so adding those together gives me 105. So, the notebooks cost her $105 in total.\n\nNow, I need to find the overall total she spent. That would be the cost of the pens plus the cost of the notebooks. So, I add $60 and $105 together. Let me add those: 60 + 105. 60 plus 100 is 160, and then plus 5 is 165. So, the total she spent is $165.\n\nShe paid with a $500 bill, so to find out how much change she gets, I subtract the total she spent from $500. So, that's 500 - 165. Let me do that subtraction. 500 minus 100 is 400, and then minus 65 more. So, 400 minus 65 is 335. Therefore, the change she should receive is $335.\n\nWait, let me double-check my calculations to make sure I didn't make a mistake. So, pens: 12 * 5 is 60. Notebooks: 5 * 21 is 105. Total: 60 + 105 is 165. Then, 500 - 165 is 335. Yeah, that seems right.\n\nAlternatively, I can think of it as 500 minus 165. Maybe breaking it down differently: 165 is 100 + 60 + 5. So, subtracting 100 from 500 gives 400, subtracting 60 gives 340, and subtracting 5 gives 335. Yep, same result.\n\nI don't think I made any errors here. So, the change Alice receives is $335.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe change Alice receives is \\boxed{335} dollars.\n\n\nAlice buys 12 pens and 5 notebooks. The cost of each pen is $5, and the cost of each notebook is $21. \n\nFirst, calculate the total cost of the pens:\n\\[\n12 \\times 5 = 60 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate the total cost of the notebooks:\n\\[\n5 \\times 21 = 105 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nAdd the total costs of pens and notebooks to find the overall total spent:\n\\[\n60 + 105 = 165 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nSubtract the total amount spent from the $500 bill to find the change:\n\\[\n500 - 165 = 335 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nThus, the change Alice receives is \\boxed{335} dollars.","logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":68,"completion_tokens":843,"total_tokens":911},"geulpu":{"seed":13697943802217284587,"tokens":[151648,198,32313,11,773,358,1184,311,7071,700,1246,1753,2297,29405,5221,1283,11833,22601,323,78531,13,6771,752,1490,13,576,3491,2727,429,22601,2783,400,20,1817,323,78531,2783,400,17,16,1817,13,29405,49531,220,16,17,22601,323,220,20,78531,323,21241,448,264,400,20,15,15,4031,13,358,1184,311,1477,700,1246,1753,2297,1340,21189,382,5338,11,358,1265,11047,279,2790,2783,315,279,22601,13,8704,1817,5750,374,400,20,323,1340,49531,220,16,17,315,1105,11,358,646,30270,220,16,17,553,220,20,13,6771,752,3270,429,1495,25,220,16,17,353,220,20,13,88190,11,220,16,17,3039,220,20,374,220,21,15,13,2055,11,279,22601,2783,1059,400,21,15,304,2790,382,5847,11,358,1184,311,11047,279,2790,2783,315,279,78531,13,8886,37166,374,400,17,16,11,323,1340,49531,220,20,315,1105,13,2055,11,358,1265,30270,220,20,553,220,17,16,13,6771,752,653,429,25,220,20,353,220,17,16,13,88190,11,220,20,3039,220,17,15,374,220,16,15,15,11,323,220,20,3039,220,16,374,220,20,11,773,7842,1846,3786,6696,752,220,16,15,20,13,2055,11,279,78531,2783,1059,400,16,15,20,304,2790,382,7039,11,358,1184,311,1477,279,8084,2790,1340,7391,13,2938,1035,387,279,2783,315,279,22601,5519,279,2783,315,279,78531,13,2055,11,358,912,400,21,15,323,4